# ─── Forward-looking scaffold ────────────────────────────────
# IMPORTANT: no code in netlify/functions/ currently reads any of these keys.
# They exist to establish the env convention ahead of the planned additions
# (CORS tightening, upstream proxy fallback, per-call timeout tuning). When
# a function is updated to consume one of these, default the value to the
# current hardcoded behavior so missing env doesn't break a deploy.
#
# Copy this file to .env (gitignored) and fill in real values.

# ─── Routing / CORS ───────────────────────────────────────────
# Optional: lock down Access-Control-Allow-Origin for fetch-data / fetch-crude.
# Leave unset to keep the current "*" (open) behavior.
# ALLOWED_ORIGIN=https://your-dashboard.example.com

# ─── Optional upstream proxies ────────────────────────────────
# If RBI / Yahoo / PPAC start blocking direct calls from the function region,
# point at a proxy you control. Leave unset to hit hosts directly.
# RBI_BASE_URL=https://www.rbi.org.in
# YAHOO_BASE_URL=https://query1.finance.yahoo.com
# PPAC_BASE_URL=https://ppac.gov.in

# ─── Sync write path ─────────────────────────────────────────
# Optional: makes every write to /data-sync require this token as the
# x-sync-token header (401 otherwise). Read by netlify/functions/data-sync.js.
#
# Worth setting on a public deploy. Without it the write path is open by design
# — the dashboard sends the token from localStorage("rbi-sync-token") when one is
# set — and while the function validates and sanitises everything it stores,
# validation stops markup but not a well-formed false record. A token is the only
# thing that keeps wrong numbers out of the shared cache.
# SYNC_WRITE_TOKEN=

# ─── Function tuning ──────────────────────────────────────────
# Per-function HTTP timeout in milliseconds (must be ≤ 26000 for Netlify free tier).
# HTTP_REQUEST_TIMEOUT_MS=10000
# YAHOO_REQUEST_TIMEOUT_MS=6000
